  "id": "motor-learning",
  "term": "motor learning",
  "definition": "Motor learning is the process of improving and retaining movement skills over time, and it is a major focus in rehabilitation after neurological injury. In this framework, it unfolds across stages such as acquiring a skill, consolidating it, and later retaining it in memory.",
